    "finding": "Empirical analysis reveals that the 65.0% Top-1 accuracy ceiling is NOT caused by ranking heuristics or mathematical scoring flaws. Modifying alpha weights from pure max-similarity (1.0) to pure centroid (0.0) yields an identical 65.0% Top-1 accuracy across all 20 independent specimens.",
    "root_bottleneck": "The root bottleneck is Reference Gallery Sparsity (N=4 images per monument). The 4 gallery images represent canonical, sunny daytime frontal viewpoints. Real-world holdout specimens include night celebrations (Shivaratri), macro stone wheel carvings (Konark hub), telephoto calligraphic friezes (Qutub), and skyward vertical angles (Victoria Memorial). A single global CLIP embedding cannot generalize to radical viewpoint shifts without visual reference coverage.",
    "proven_safety_invariant": "Crucially, the Phase 6.2 Uncertainty Engine flawlessly safeguards the system: 0 false matches were accepted, with all 7 ambiguous specimens gated into UNCERTAIN_MATCH, REVIEW_REQUIRED, or NON_MONUMENT_REJECTED. Lowering thresholds would artificially inflate accuracy while destroying curatorial safety.",
